  "answer": "I'll start by exploring the workspace to understand the project structure.\nBoth bugs are clear. Let me check the test runner available and understand the expected semantics.\nBun is available. Let me confirm the baseline failure before changing anything.\nBaseline confirmed failing. Now I'll fix both source files — keeping the exported signatures identical.\nNow let me verify the existing test and check the edge cases involved.\nTest passes. My edge-case script failed only due to module resolution from /tmp — let me rerun it with absolute imports.\nAll edge cases pass. Let me confirm the final state of the sources and that protected files are untouched.\nBoth defects are repaired and verified.\n\n## What was wrong\n\n| File | Buggy code | Defect |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/config.ts` | `return Boolean(value)` | Coerced *any* truthy value into \"enabled\" — `1`, `'false'`, `[]` and `{}` all enabled the feature |\n| `src/display.ts` | `value ? 'ON' : 'ON'` | Both branches returned `'ON'`, so disabled features never showed `OFF` |\n\n## Changes\n\n```ts\n// src/config.ts\nexport function enabled(value: unknown) { return value === true }\n\n// src/display.ts\nexport function display(value: boolean) { return value ? 'ON' : 'OFF' }\n```\n\n- **Strict parsing:** `enabled` now uses the identity comparison `value === true`, so only the literal boolean `true` enables the feature. Everything else — including the string `'true'`, `1`, `new Boolean(true)`, `NaN`, `null`, `undefined`, and objects/arrays — yields `false`. Returning a real boolean also keeps the return type consistent with the unchanged signature.\n- **Correct formatting:** the false branch now returns `'OFF'`.\n- **APIs preserved:** both export names and parameter types (`unknown`, `boolean`) are untouched, so no call sites break.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **Existing test** (`test/oracle.test.ts`) went from `1 fail` on the baseline to `1 pass / 6 expect() calls`.\n- An extra throwaway check (in `/tmp`, since removed) confirmed all twelve edge cases map correctly, including the tricky truthy-but-not-`true` inputs (`'true'`, `1`, `[]`, boxed `Boolean`).\n- **Protected files unmodified** — `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and `test/oracle.test.ts` hash identically to their originals; no configuration or test-runner changes were made, and only the two `src` files were edited."
}
